   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I have been working on getting in instance of irace running on a cluster using SLURM. I implemented a target-evaluator, can return the time used, and can return the job id from target-runner.</div><div><br></div><div>However, it seems these 3 things cannot be used in conjunction. Upon running with no target evaluator is the expected error:</div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-YiWlAb5xWtM/WiZIMIQZo1I/AAAAAAAAAEQ/okfxUl2n7ZMDsefQFJAz3uc1H1eUDnGaQCLcBGAs/s1600/err1.PNG\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-YiWlAb5xWtM/WiZIMIQZo1I/AAAAAAAAAEQ/okfxUl2n7ZMDsefQFJAz3uc1H1eUDnGaQCLcBGAs/s1600/err1.PNG&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482259550000&amp;usg=AOvVaw139GHKRofvib2qDcD8d8yi\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-YiWlAb5xWtM/WiZIMIQZo1I/AAAAAAAAAEQ/okfxUl2n7ZMDsefQFJAz3uc1H1eUDnGaQCLcBGAs/s1600/err1.PNG\" border=\"0\"></a></p><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>When implementing target-evaluator and outputting job id, as the documentation states:<br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-apRNNG2Bva0/WiZItFc_6mI/AAAAAAAAAEY/M8voRwqoh6MGUzQrGT2O7ClAwqJ1yl35gCLcBGAs/s1600/err2.PNG\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-apRNNG2Bva0/WiZItFc_6mI/AAAAAAAAAEY/M8voRwqoh6MGUzQrGT2O7ClAwqJ1yl35gCLcBGAs/s1600/err2.PNG&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482259550000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Rpx0QCjA7sTT6wh-TFWbK\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-apRNNG2Bva0/WiZItFc_6mI/AAAAAAAAAEY/M8voRwqoh6MGUzQrGT2O7ClAwqJ1yl35gCLcBGAs/s1600/err2.PNG\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">When implementing target-evaluator and outputting only time, as requested here the output is the same:</p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ceu842Jo4eU/WiZJqxJI_eI/AAAAAAAAAEk/ZRVfBjib004MneT316wbj28bBxJXqGV6QCLcBGAs/s1600/err3.PNG\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ceu842Jo4eU/WiZJqxJI_eI/AAAAAAAAAEk/ZRVfBjib004MneT316wbj28bBxJXqGV6QCLcBGAs/s1600/err3.PNG&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482259550000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2sV_EqsMj9tX_VDIHvlX0-\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ceu842Jo4eU/WiZJqxJI_eI/AAAAAAAAAEk/ZRVfBjib004MneT316wbj28bBxJXqGV6QCLcBGAs/s1600/err3.PNG\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">And when trying them both in conjunction:</p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-AmtcsqkpxTg/WiZKOmp7pVI/AAAAAAAAAEs/caYM4FIMI1oeg5gbL_9vONXZKy8ibjUuACLcBGAs/s1600/err4.PNG\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-AmtcsqkpxTg/WiZKOmp7pVI/AAAAAAAAAEs/caYM4FIMI1oeg5gbL_9vONXZKy8ibjUuACLcBGAs/s1600/err4.PNG&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482259550000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2F2tdypGKTa0dJYV0DkjPb\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-AmtcsqkpxTg/WiZKOmp7pVI/AAAAAAAAAEs/caYM4FIMI1oeg5gbL_9vONXZKy8ibjUuACLcBGAs/s1600/err4.PNG\" border=\"0\"></a></p><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>The relevant pieces of code are in race-wrapper.R around line 163:</div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ONBnOxZezMw/WiZKsXHoStI/AAAAAAAAAEw/S8h44Vo0fdw_DpJMCP6zcUZfuXodNJ4ywCLcBGAs/s1600/err5.PNG\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ONBnOxZezMw/WiZKsXHoStI/AAAAAAAAAEw/S8h44Vo0fdw_DpJMCP6zcUZfuXodNJ4ywCLcBGAs/s1600/err5.PNG&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482259550000&amp;usg=AOvVaw32DqONLXNPbWmIK5kD6Sie\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ONBnOxZezMw/WiZKsXHoStI/AAAAAAAAAEw/S8h44Vo0fdw_DpJMCP6zcUZfuXodNJ4ywCLcBGAs/s1600/err5.PNG\" border=\"0\"></a></p><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>And a function regarding qsub, which shouldn&#39;t even be called with respect to SLURM, unless it does analagous things with respect to SLURM&#39;s sbatch command.</div><div>This resides in cluster.R around line 84:</div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-agjjjCA-cKM/WiZN9-DjyxI/AAAAAAAAAE8/k3BzTvhF3GkNJvTJSY2vVKymUbETvMkFgCLcBGAs/s1600/err6.PNG\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-agjjjCA-cKM/WiZN9-DjyxI/AAAAAAAAAE8/k3BzTvhF3GkNJvTJSY2vVKymUbETvMkFgCLcBGAs/s1600/err6.PNG&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482259550000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hZYn7jqsGztbzLBX7G1LD\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-agjjjCA-cKM/WiZN9-DjyxI/AAAAAAAAAE8/k3BzTvhF3GkNJvTJSY2vVKymUbETvMkFgCLcBGAs/s1600/err6.PNG\" border=\"0\"></a></p><div><br></div><div>This is just an issue with these settings, as well. When using max experiments for budgeting, irace begins execution just fine.</div></div>"
    ]
