   "date": "2017-12-06T09:27:53Z",
   "subject": "Re: Potential batchmode bug",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<br><br>Yes, the problem is that with --maxTime, irace assumes that target-runner will report the time, however, this is not possible with --batchmode. It is possible to fix this but it will not be a one-liner so it will take me some days. If you are confident in modifying the package sources, you need to add a check on scenario$batchmode before checking the scenario$maxTime condition that you quote, you need to handle the case where that function returns no time and you need to handle the case that target-evaluator returns time and how to use that to increment the time budget.<br><br>In the meantime, I would suggest that you don&#39;t use --maxTime for now.<br><br>Cheers,<br><br>Manuel.</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Tuesday, 5 December 2017 09:55:08 UTC+2, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dmh...@mst.edu</a>  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I have been working on getting in instance of irace running on a cluster using SLURM. I implemented a target-evaluator, can return the time used, and can return the job id from target-runner.</div><div><br></div><div>However, it seems these 3 things cannot be used in conjunction. Upon running with no target evaluator is the expected error:</div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-YiWlAb5xWtM/WiZIMIQZo1I/AAAAAAAAAEQ/okfxUl2n7ZMDsefQFJAz3uc1H1eUDnGaQCLcBGAs/s1600/err1.PNG\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-YiWlAb5xWtM/WiZIMIQZo1I/AAAAAAAAAEQ/okfxUl2n7ZMDsefQFJAz3uc1H1eUDnGaQCLcBGAs/s1600/err1.PNG&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482259554000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2td35yGlXRsV77ib3gM-tc\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-YiWlAb5xWtM/WiZIMIQZo1I/AAAAAAAAAEQ/okfxUl2n7ZMDsefQFJAz3uc1H1eUDnGaQCLcBGAs/s1600/err1.PNG\" border=\"0\"></a></p><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>When implementing target-evaluator and outputting job id, as the documentation states:<br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-apRNNG2Bva0/WiZItFc_6mI/AAAAAAAAAEY/M8voRwqoh6MGUzQrGT2O7ClAwqJ1yl35gCLcBGAs/s1600/err2.PNG\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-apRNNG2Bva0/WiZItFc_6mI/AAAAAAAAAEY/M8voRwqoh6MGUzQrGT2O7ClAwqJ1yl35gCLcBGAs/s1600/err2.PNG&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482259554000&amp;usg=AOvVaw11ugqqGD